<h3>Creating Your Account & Getting Started</h3>
<p>You can register with email/password, Google, Facebook, TikTok, or a WhatsApp OTP (no email needed). During registration you pick which modules interest you — Nikah Matchmaking, Quran Learning, Digital Skills, Family Counseling — and land straight in that area. If you arrived from a shared link (e.g. someone's Nikah profile, a course page, a blog post) and had to log in or register first, you're sent right back to that exact page afterward.</p>
<p>Turn any module on or off anytime from <strong>Profile → Module Preferences</strong> — this only changes what shows in your navigation and dashboard, it never deletes anything you've already created there.</p>

<h3>Dashboard</h3>
<p>Your stat tiles (enrollments, live classes, unread notifications) link straight to the relevant page. The <strong>Notifications</strong> panel lists every update across every module — new Nikah interest, approved post, confirmed payment, class assignment, and more — with "Mark all read." <strong>Quick Links</strong> adapts to whichever modules you've enabled.</p>

<h3>👤 Profile Settings</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Basic info</strong>: name, email/phone, gender, city, profile photo.</li>
    <li><strong>Public Author Profile</strong>: an optional public username and a short bio (shown on any Community Post you publish and on your public author page).</li>
    <li><strong>WhatsApp notifications</strong>: opt in to receive updates by WhatsApp in addition to email/in-app.</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter</strong>: opt out anytime — an unsubscribe link is also in every newsletter email.</li>
    <li><strong>Module Preferences</strong>: toggle Nikah/Quran/Skills/Counseling on or off.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete Account</strong>: permanently remove your account and data.</li>
</ul>

<h3>💍 Nikah Matchmaking</h3>
<p>Creating a profile is a 5-step guided wizard — you can save progress and finish later:</p>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Basic Info</strong> — age, height, marital status, education, profession, city, country/state.</li>
    <li><strong>Family & Background</strong> — caste, family type, guardian name/contact/relation, ethnicity, languages spoken.</li>
    <li><strong>Deen & Lifestyle</strong> — sect, prayer regularity, hijab/beard, smoking, diet, openness to polygamy.</li>
    <li><strong>About & Preferences</strong> — about you, what you're looking for, and preferences for a match (age range, city, sect, education, marital status).</li>
    <li><strong>Photos & Verification</strong> — CNIC number + front/back photos (required), an optional profile photo, whether to allow your photo to be shared after mutual interest, and profile visibility (four levels — see below).</li>
</ol>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Verification is mandatory</strong> — your profile isn't visible to anyone until an admin verifies your CNIC and your one-time verification fee payment is confirmed (submit via JazzCash/Easypaisa/bank transfer + screenshot).</li>
    <li><strong>Profile Visibility — four levels, your choice</strong>: <em>Anyone can find me</em> (shows in Browse and in Google search results); <em>Sallaamti members only</em> (shows in Browse, but not on Google); <em>Only my matchmaker can find me</em> (hidden from everyone browsing — a matchmaker assisting you can still find and suggest you); <em>Nobody can find me by searching</em> (fully hidden from all search/browse — only someone who already has your exact profile, like a matchmaker you've spoken to directly, can work with it). You can change this anytime from your profile's Edit page.</li>
    <li><strong>Browse</strong> shows opposite-gender, verified, active profiles set to "Anyone can find me" or "Sallaamti members only" that match your filters. <strong>Saved Profiles</strong> lets you bookmark ones to revisit.</li>
    <li><strong>Interest</strong>: send interest to start things off; the other person can Accept or Decline. Once accepted, a guardian-to-guardian messaging thread opens up for the two families to talk directly and safely.</li>
    <li><strong>Safety</strong>: Block or Report any profile from their page, anytime. A blocked profile can never see or contact you again. You can also deactivate your own profile temporarily.</li>
    <li><strong>Sharing your profile</strong>: every verified profile has a safe public preview link (no photos, no guardian contact shown) you can share on WhatsApp — this always works no matter which visibility level you've chosen, since it's the only way anyone can view a profile that isn't set to "Anyone can find me."</li>
</ul>

<h3>📖 Quran Courses (Self-Paced)</h3>
<p>Browse published courses by category, work through lessons (text/video content) at your own pace, and take the quiz at the end to earn a certificate — downloadable as a PDF with a QR code anyone can scan to independently verify it's genuine. Track your progress under <strong>My Learning</strong>.</p>

<h3>🎥 Quran Live Classes</h3>
<p>Admission is a 3-step wizard, one per child if you're enrolling more than one:</p>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Parent & Contact</strong> — your name, WhatsApp number, country/city.</li>
    <li><strong>About the Student</strong> — student's name, gender, age, education grade, whether they've learned Quran before.</li>
    <li><strong>Class Preferences</strong> — preferred days/time, timezone, teacher gender preference, which level, previous level completed, one-to-one vs. group class, and any special notes.</li>
</ol>
<ul>
    <li>After admission, submit your <strong>monthly subscription payment</strong> — once an admin confirms it, your daily class link appears under <strong>My Quran Class</strong>, refreshed by your teacher every class day.</li>
    <li>Message your child's teacher directly from the class page.</li>
    <li>View <strong>My Progress</strong> for assessments and monthly progress reports the teacher files for your child.</li>
</ul>

<h3>💻 Digital Skills</h3>
<p>Works exactly like self-paced Quran courses (lessons, quiz, certificate) — practical tech skills content presented by IZMA Digital Technology & Security.</p>

<h3>🤝 Volunteering</h3>
<p>Anyone can apply, with or without an account. Fields: name, email, phone, city, area of interest, and a short message. If approved and you have an account (or create one with the same email afterward), you automatically get the Volunteer role and an official Volunteer ID Card emailed to you as a PDF, with a QR code anyone can scan to verify your status. You'll be notified either way — approved or not.</p>

<h3>💰 Donations</h3>
<p>Also open to guests. Fill in an amount, payment method (bank transfer/international), your name and email (optional if you want a receipt/updates), the cause, an optional message, and whether to stay anonymous. Upload a payment screenshot if you have one. Track your donation history under <strong>My Donations</strong> if you're logged in.</p>

<h3>🗓️ Family Counseling</h3>
<p>Browse available counselors and their public bios, pick an open time slot, and book. You'll be notified when the counselor confirms, replies, completes, or cancels the session. Message the counselor directly from your booking if you need to share more context beforehand.</p>

<h3>🤲 Sallaamti Wall</h3>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Dua Requests</strong> — submit a request for prayers (with an option to post anonymously); it's reviewed by our team before appearing publicly, so the feed stays genuine.</li>
    <li><strong>Community Posts</strong> — admin-published activities, events, and announcements.</li>
    <li>React (multiple reaction types) and comment (one reply level deep) on anything approved/published. <strong>Saved</strong> lets you bookmark posts to find again later. Filter the feed by tag.</li>
</ul>

<h3>📝 Community Posts (Share Your Story)</h3>
<p>Anyone with an account can write a post — a story, reflection, or announcement — under <strong>Community Posts → Share Your Story</strong>.</p>
<ul>
    <li>Fields: title, an optional short summary (auto-generated from your text if left blank), your post body, and an optional cover image.</li>
    <li>Unless you hold staff permissions, your post goes to <strong>pending review</strong> first — you'll get a notification once an admin approves or rejects it (with a reason, if rejected).</li>
    <li>Once published, it gets its own permanent shareable web address, showing your name and short public bio, with one-click buttons to share it on WhatsApp, Facebook, or X — plus a "Copy Link" button.</li>
    <li>Editing an already-published post sends it back for review again, so the review step stays meaningful.</li>
    <li><strong>My Posts</strong> shows every post you've written with its current status (Pending/Published/Rejected), views count, and Edit/Delete actions.</li>
</ul>

<h3>📰 Blog</h3>
<p>Read-only long-form articles written by our content team.</p>

<h3>🎓 Certificates</h3>
<p><strong>My Certificates</strong> lists every certificate you've earned (course completions, Volunteer ID) — each downloads as a PDF and can be verified independently at the public certificate-verification page using its certificate number or QR code.</p>

<h3>💬 Support & Contact</h3>
<p>Submit a Family Support query if you need help from our team on something personal or sensitive — it gets assigned to a counselor/staff member who replies through a private thread, with status updates (New → Assigned → In Progress → Resolved). The general <strong>Contact</strong> form on the website is for anything else.</p>

</div>

